      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The raw energy of Wild Style established a template for authentic hip-hop storytelling that influenced generations. While Hollywood produced polished but shallow films like <a href=\"/movie/15259\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"15259\">Breakin'</a> (1984) and Electric Boogaloo (1984), independent filmmakers followed Wild Style's documentary-like approach. <a href=\"/movie/31225\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"31225\">Paris Is Burning</a> (1990) explored voguing culture with similar authenticity, while <a href=\"/movie/18984\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"18984\">Scratch</a> (2001) paid tribute to hip-hop's DJ pioneers."
      }
